From 2edb486e21159db5333e2a0763ca901c7bb096b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 19:24:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] latex-lab: float target \@floatHref@<type>

latex-lab-float gave some captions in tagged floats a link target that
is never made, because its plug of caption/step rebuilt the name from
\@captype and \@current@float@struct when the caption was stepped:

- after \tagpdfsetup{float/split} the target of the split is
  floatstructure.<n>, but the caption used <type>.struct.<n> with the
  new number ("name{figure.struct.<n>} has been referenced but does not
  exist");
- a table caption inside a figure (\def\@captype{table}) used
  table.struct.<n>, which does not exist either.

The float code now stores the target in \@floatHref@<type>, locally
inside the float box: at the start of the float (\@currentHref after
\MakeLinkTarget*, so a renaming by target/setname/after is respected;
before the hook float/begin) and after float/split. The kernel plug of
caption/step already uses it, so the plug latex-lab is removed. As the
type is part of the name, a table caption inside a figure gets a target
of its own (table.1), and so does a caption outside of floats, where the
name is undefined. \@floatHref@<type> is documented as the float target
that other code (e.g., the caption package) may read.

The structure-name helper also falls back to float/generic when
\@captype is undefined (\@makecaption used outside of floats by
packages gave an undefined control sequence).

Tests: new latex-lab float-023 (targets at the float start, after
float/split, table caption in a figure, \caption* in a float, captions
outside of floats, continued captions in and outside of floats,
\@makecaption with \@captype undefined); float-004 (a caption after
float/split) now links to floatstructure.<n>.
